dialogue vane
  node root vane "Clerks don't steer. Say what you came to say and be off my deck."
    > "About your three terms." if vane_terms -> count
    > "Your course is the long way round." if looked:marrow_cabin.chart and not vane_terms -> course
    > "What happened to the other ships?" -> ships
    > "Where's your navigator?" if not seen:vane.pell -> pell
    > "Nothing, captain." -> bye
  node pell vane "Pell. Forty years at sea. Died in his hammock last winter, mid-sentence. I'd give a great deal to know how that sentence ended."
    > "What happened to the other ships?" -> ships
    > "I'm sorry." -> bye
  node course vane "We sail Pell's line, north of the reef. Two days longer and nobody's ever been lost on it. Nobody runs the south side. Nobody who comes back."
    > "What if there's a way through?" -> through
    > "Understood, captain." -> bye
  node through vane "Then show me on the chart, clerk, with something better than hope. I've a hold full of hope already and it pays terribly."
    > "Yes, captain." -> bye
  node ships vane "Six ships in three years. Five found drifting, holds empty, not a soul aboard. The sixth was the Arcadia, and nobody found so much as a plank."
    -> insurers
  node insurers vane "The insurers paid on all six, for weather. That same year they refused my claim for a real storm."
    -> funny
  node funny vane "Funny thing, weather."
    > "Who are you carrying for now?" if not seen:vane.cray -> cray
    > "Where's your navigator?" if not seen:vane.pell -> pell
    > "I'll let you get on." -> bye
  node cray vane "Cray's charter. Cray's crates. Cray's money, the only kind that still hires me. …It pays for the stew, clerk. Some of us eat."
    > "Where's your navigator?" if not seen:vane.pell -> pell
    > "I'll let you get on." -> bye
  node count vane "A navigator, a crew, and a reason Pell would have. Count them for me, clerk. Slowly."
    > "Quill has sworn to the line." if quill_navigator -> quill
    > "The crew will sail it." if crew_agree -> crew
    > "Still counting." -> counting
  node quill vane "Quill. Pell said she had the best eyes he ever saw and the worst patience. He'd have liked this. He'd have pretended not to."
    > "The crew will sail it." if crew_agree -> crew
    > "That's one." -> counting
  node crew vane "Hobb told me. He rolled up his sleeve to do it. In nine years I've never seen his whole arm."
    > "That's two." -> counting
  node counting vane "And a reason Pell would have. Pell never said anything he hadn't written down first, clerk. Off you go."
  node bye vane "Off my deck, clerk."
  # The compass on the chart (rooms.ts) opens here.
  node compass vane "Through the reef. There is no way through the reef, clerk. That's what a reef is."
    > "My father found one." -> father
  node father vane "And who is your father, that he finds holes in reefs?"
    > "Ansel Fenn. Of the Arcadia." -> ansel
  node ansel vane "Ansel Fenn ran the Straits in half the time of anyone alive, and never told a soul how. The old men in the Keel talk about a straight gap through that reef. The Needle."
    -> ansel2
  node ansel2 vane "I took it for a story for selling drinks. …So. That's how."
    -> needle
  node needle narrator "She looks at the needle for a long moment. The needle looks back, unrepentant."
    -> no
  node no vane "No. A dead man's compass and a clerk's word. I buried one navigator this winter. I'm not drowning a ship for a second."
    > "Then what would it take?" -> terms
      set vane_terms
    > "I could fill in a form." -> form
      set vane_terms
    > "He isn't dead, captain. He's overdue." -> overdue
  node overdue vane "…Spoken like a man who's never had to write the other word."
    > "Then what would it take?" -> terms
      set vane_terms
    > "I could fill in a form." -> form
      set vane_terms
  node form vane "If a form could get a ship through that reef, clerk, Silas Cray would own the reef by now. …No. Here's what it would take."
    -> terms
  node terms vane "Three things. A navigator who'll swear to that line. A crew who'll sail it."
    -> terms2
  node terms2 vane "And a reason Pell would have. Pell never dared the south side, clerk. Give me a reason he would have."
    > "Yes, captain." -> END
    > "Three things. I've done harder lists before breakfast." -> lists
  node lists vane "It's past breakfast. Go and eat something; Dorrit's been sulking at the stew since Port Vela."
  # Pell's log, given once the other two terms are met (rooms.ts, marrow_cabin).
  node log fenn "Pell's last entry. It doesn't finish."
    -> there
  node there vane "I know. I was there."
    > "You said you'd give a great deal to know how it ended." if seen:vane.pell -> read
    > "May I read it to you?" -> read
  node read fenn "“If Ansel's boy ever comes aboard with the old man's compass, tell the captain she should…”"
    -> boy
  node boy narrator "Ansel's boy. Nobody has called me that in three years. I read it the way it was written, and my voice only goes once."
    -> silence
  node silence narrator "Vane is quiet for so long that the ship's timbers start talking to fill the gap."
    -> trust
  node trust vane "Trust the boy. That's how it ends. Pell and Ansel Fenn drank the same bad rum every winter for twenty years. Of course Ansel told him."
    -> trust2
  node trust2 vane "And Pell never told me, because I never trusted anyone."
    -> hat
  node hat narrator "She stands, and puts on her hat, which I gather is serious."
    -> coward
  node coward vane "Fine. Forty years, Pell, and you finally give an order, and you make me finish it for you."
    -> orders
  node orders vane "Get to the bow, clerk. Quill takes the wheel. You call the bearings. And if you're wrong, call them louder."
    > "Aye, captain." -> END
      take pell_log
      set vane_convinced
    > "I've never said “aye” before." -> aye
      take pell_log
      set vane_convinced
  node aye vane "You'll get the hang of it. Most people do by the second reef."
